From 30f7cdeacbb5e7ea7ed1a9c083c5f236ccbedf92 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Emmanuel Blot <emmanuel.blot@free.fr>
Date: Fri, 7 Aug 2026 18:03:29 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] hw/arm: ventura: populate the FRU EEPROMs

Back the seven FRU EEPROMs with images read from hardware, so guest
firmware can identify the RMC, SCM, BSM, LED, rear I/O and the two fan
boards instead of finding blank EEPROMs and refusing to enumerate
them.

The content is sanitized, not real hardware data: part and serial
numbers are masked, manufacturing dates fixed, asset tags replaced and
custom fields cleared apart from the MAC addresses, which keep their
OUI and are renumbered. The area layout is preserved, so anything that
parses the IPMI FRU structure sees a faithful image.

Each fan board carries its own FRU, so the shared initialiser now
takes the image to install.

Signed-off-by: Emmanuel Blot <emmanuel.blot@free.fr>
---
 hw/arm/aspeed_ast2600_ventura.c | 271 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 262 insertions(+), 9 deletions(-)

diff --git a/hw/arm/aspeed_ast2600_ventura.c b/hw/arm/aspeed_ast2600_ventura.c
index 11c823279f..931eb43803 100644
